C13 round 4 done. Local Git Bash only, no host, no network, nothing committed.

**Fix (RP6-P0.sh, `p0_resolve_passwd`)** — plain `$( … )` ate trailing newlines, so newline-only rc-2 read as empty → false no-match. Now:
```bash
raw="$(LC_ALL=C "$P0_GETENT" passwd "$acct" 2>&1 || getent_rc=$?; printf x; exit "${getent_rc:-0}")" || rc=$?
case "$raw" in *x) raw="${raw%x}" ;; *) P0_PW_DIAG="capture_sentinel_lost"; P0_PW_OUTCOME="error"; return 0 ;; esac
[ -z "$raw" ] || had_bytes=yes
while [ "${raw%$'\n'}" != "$raw" ]; do raw="${raw%$'\n'}"; done
```
- getent rc carried out by re-exiting subshell (printf's rc would mask it — kickoff's warning).
- getent on left of `||` so inherited `set -e` can't kill subshell before sentinel (that failure would be silent + fail-OPEN). Verified empirically under `set -Eeuo pipefail`.
- Sentinel missing → `error`/`capture_sentinel_lost`, fail closed.
- After the emptiness decision `raw` normalized back to the pre-repair value → rc-0 record parse and all diag strings byte-identical to R3.
- Newline-only rc-2 → `error` / `newline_only_capture_at_rc2` → caller `identity_unresolvable` rc 3.

**Same-pattern sweep:** only one rc-2-adjudicated site in the file (one `2)` arm). Other captures treat any non-zero rc as error; other emptiness tests fail CLOSED (`p0_capture_numeric` → `p0_stop identity_probe_empty`). No other site changed.

